{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DvTemkh4sf4SitvVLR5Dkv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage bddgo\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"errors\"\n5\t\t\"fmt\"\n6\t\t\"strings\"\n7\t\t\"testing\"\n8\t)\n9\t\n10\t// ErrScenarioNotInRegistry signals a generated test naming a scenario\n11\t// the registry does not hold — a scenario deleted without regenerating.\n12\tvar ErrScenarioNotInRegistry = errors.New(\"no scenario in the registry has this id\")\n13\t\n14\t// ErrScenarioNotOwned signals a generated test compiled into a suite\n15\t// whose service the scenario does not name. It would otherwise run\n16\t// against a state built for a different surface entirely.\n17\tvar ErrScenarioNotOwned = errors.New(\"this suite does not own that scenario\")\n18\t\n19\t// ErrModifierWithoutBlock signals And/But before any Given/When/Then. A\n20\t// modifier inherits the block above it; with nothing above, there is\n21\t// nothing to inherit and no way to tell whether the step acts or asserts.\n22\tvar ErrModifierWithoutBlock = errors.New(\"And/But before any Given/When/Then\")\n23\t\n24\t// ErrScenarioDrift signals a generated test file whose steps are not the\n25\t// registry's — refused whole rather than run partially, since a scenario\n26\t// that runs the file's steps but reports the registry's is worse.\n27\tvar ErrScenarioDrift = errors.New(\"the registry and this generated test file disagree\")\n28\t\n29\t// ErrDoneTwice signals Done called more than once on one scenario.\n30\tvar ErrDoneTwice = errors.New(\"Done was already called\")\n31\t\n32\t// regenerate names the command that reconciles a drifted file. Quoted\n33\t// into every drift failure, because the fix is never a hand edit.\n34\tconst regenerate = \"true-bdd build tests --fix\"\n35\t\n36\t// Run is one scenario as its generated test file drives it: the file\n37\t// declares steps via Given/When/Then/And/But, Done runs them, and the\n38\t// registry supplies id/description/b